    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "c882bdda56bd72d0",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "c882bdda56bd72d0",
        "text": "A ledger with linked entries shows a badge: **Verified** (green) when every linked entry is matched, **Partly verified** (orange) when some are, **Not verified** (red) when none are or a counterparty page cannot be reached. Hover for the detail: how many matched, which entries did not and where the plugin looked. The counterparty page is found by its `LEDGER:` hint, else on this page's own site, else on any neighbourhood site whose sitemap lists it. The check runs in the browser; the last result is kept on the item as `item.verified`."
      },
      "after": "2565e0c18332453d",
      "date": 1790161690359,
      "provenance": "Authored by an AI agent \u2014 Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5) executing the [[Timebank Verification Plan]]."
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "39023f1c68d65c2a",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "39023f1c68d65c2a",
        "text": "# Notify Topic\nClick the badge to ask for confirmation"
      },
      "after": "c882bdda56bd72d0",
      "date": 1790161690359,
      "provenance": "Authored by an AI agent \u2014 Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5) executing the [[Timebank Verification Plan]]."
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "d7a03d9baa6c3c14",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "d7a03d9baa6c3c14",
        "text": "A single click on the badge re-runs the check. With a `NOTIFY:` line it then posts one message per counterparty to that [https://ntfy.sh ntfy] topic: the title names the ledger, the tags carry the status, the click link opens the counterparty page, and the body lists each entry as `Confirmed: \u2026 \u2014 matched` or `Verify: \u2026 \u2014 unmatched in site/slug`. The tooltip then says sent or send failed. Without a `NOTIFY:` line the click only re-verifies. Double-click anywhere else on the ledger still opens the editor."
      },
      "after": "39023f1c68d65c2a",
      "date": 1790161690359,
      "provenance": "Authored by an AI agent \u2014 Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5) executing the [[Timebank Verification Plan]]."
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "21341e728c47230c",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "21341e728c47230c",
        "text": "The TimeBank plugin displays a list of time entries as a dated ledger. Each line in the item text is one entry. Lines ending with a time amount are summed into a running total. The column header shows the end date of the batch. An entry can name a counterparty ledger \u2014 `Gardening for [[Alice Ledger]]: 2 hours` on the same site, or `Gardening for [https://alice.wiki/view/alices-ledger Alice's Ledger]: 2 hours` on another site \u2014 and a **Verified** badge checks that the other ledger records the same hours the other way round. Clicking the badge opens a **Ledger Verification Tool** page beside the ledger. Labels and captions go through the wiki's link resolver, so [[wikilinks]] work everywhere in the item. See [[Table Formatting]] for the HTML markup used to render the table."
      },
      "date": 1790171171301
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "c1cecc47bb6f159a",
      "item": {
        "type": "table",
        "id": "c1cecc47bb6f159a",
        "text": "CAPTION Commands are never shown as entries or caption\n\n| Command | Example | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| START: | START: 1 September 2026 | Start of the period |\n| END: | END: 7 September 2026 | End of the period, shown as the column header |\n| NOTIFY: | NOTIFY: ntfy.sh/timebank-david | The ntfy topic the tool page's Send verification message button posts to; https unless you write http:// |"
      },
      "date": 1790171171301
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "511f4abddf458ec6",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "511f4abddf458ec6",
        "text": "An entry that ends `for` or `to` a ledger records hours **I gave** to it. One that ends `from` or `by` a ledger records hours **I received**. Name a ledger on this same site with a wikilink, `for [[Alice Ledger]]`. Name a ledger on **another site** with an external link to the exact page, `for [https://alice.wiki/view/alices-ledger Alice's Ledger]` \u2014 it opens in a new tab and carries the site in its address. `http://`, `//site/slug`, ports, a trailing slash and a `.html` or `.json` suffix are accepted; write `/view/slug`, because a wiki answers that address and not a bare `/slug`. The other ledger confirms an entry with the opposite word and a link back to this page. A link without a direction word \u2014 `Meeting with [[David]]: 2 hours` \u2014 is an ordinary entry that happens to contain a link. The old `LEDGER:` command is gone since 0.3.0."
      },
      "date": 1790171171301
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "46a90ffb474d085b",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "46a90ffb474d085b",
        "text": "A ledger is identified by its **site plus its slug**, never its title alone: two pages called David's Ledger on two sites are two ledgers and never match each other. A wikilink on the other ledger names the other ledger's own site, so it only points back here when both ledgers share a site; across sites the other ledger must name this one by external link. Two entries match when the other entry points back at this exact ledger, runs the opposite way, has the same minutes, and the same label once case, spacing and trailing punctuation are ignored. Each counter-entry confirms one entry only. When both items declare START/END the periods must overlap. On this about page Alice Ledger does not exist, so the badge above is red."
      },
      "date": 1790171171301
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "c882bdda56bd72d0",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "c882bdda56bd72d0",
        "text": "A ledger with linked entries shows a badge: **Verified** (green) when every linked entry is matched, **Partly verified** (orange) when some are, **Not verified** (red) when none are or a counterparty ledger cannot be reached. Hover for the detail: how many matched, which entries did not, and the address of the ledger that was checked. Each counterparty site named by external link is registered as a neighbour, so its flag shows and its pages resolve. The check runs in the browser; the last result is kept on the item as `item.verified`, with the time and the site that checked it."
      },
      "date": 1790171171301
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "39023f1c68d65c2a",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "39023f1c68d65c2a",
        "text": "# Ledger Verification Tool\nClick the badge for a page that says what was checked"
      },
      "date": 1790171171301
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "d7a03d9baa6c3c14",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "d7a03d9baa6c3c14",
        "text": "A single click on the badge re-checks and opens a Ledger Verification Tool page beside the ledger. It is generated in the browser and never stored. It names the ledger, its site, when and from where it was checked, and the status; a table lists every linked entry with its direction, hours, label, counterparty ledger and result \u2014 matched, unmatched or ledger unreachable. **Send verification message** posts one message per counterparty to the `NOTIFY:` [https://ntfy.sh ntfy] topic \u2014 title, status tags, a click link to the counterparty ledger, and a body of `Confirmed: \u2026 \u2014 matched` or `Verify: \u2026 \u2014 unmatched in <ledger address>` lines \u2014 and shows sent or send failed. **Find missing ledgers** lists, for every unreachable or unmatched counterparty, pages whose title or slug matches in the neighbourhood and on the sites this page links to. A **Fix** button beside each candidate rewrites those entry lines to name it by external link, saves the ledger and checks again; it needs the browser to be logged in as the site owner and says so when it is not. Double-click anywhere else on the ledger still opens the editor."
      },
      "date": 1790171171301
    },
    {
