    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "21341e728c47230c",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "21341e728c47230c",
        "text": "The TimeBank plugin displays a list of time entries as a dated ledger. Each line in the item text is one entry. Lines ending with a time amount are summed into a running total. The column header shows the end date of the batch. An entry can name a counterparty ledger \u2014 `Gardening for [[Alice Ledger]]: 2 hours` on the same site, or `Gardening for [https://alice.wiki/view/alices-ledger Alice's Ledger]: 2 hours` on another site \u2014 and a **Verified** badge checks that the other ledger records the same hours the other way round. Clicking the badge opens the **Ledger Verification Tool** page beside the ledger. Since 0.4.0 an entry's label can link the **Time Transaction** page that records the work, and a ledger with a `LINEUP` line pulls its entries from those pages. Labels and captions go through the wiki's link resolver, so [[wikilinks]] work everywhere in the item. See [[Table Formatting]] for the HTML markup used to render the table."
